    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 7,
    "summary": "Nephi is rejected in the north and returns to Zarahemla—He prays upon his garden tower and then calls upon the people to repent or perish. About 23–21 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [
      {
        "type": "introduction",
        "text": "Comprising chapters 7 through 16."
      }
    ],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Behold, now it came to pass in the sixty and ninth year of the reign of the judges over the people of the Nephites, that Nephi, the son of Helaman, returned to the land of Zarahemla from the land northward.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 148,
            "end": 156,
            "text": "Hel. 6:6."
          }
